orum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T01:45:18-08:00","id":1421404,"title":"","content":"I think so. They haven\u2019t done Sorcerer for M20 yet. Christopher Barrow in Dread Names, Red List extended his life thru hedge magic so there might be some rules in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T09:28:07-08:00","id":1421461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1421348-mortal-life-extension-how?p=1421404#post1421404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think so. They haven\u2019t done Sorcerer for M20 yet. Christopher Barrow in Dread Names, Red List extended his life thru hedge magic so there might be some rules in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Sorcerer Revised has life extention stuff in it and is the most up to date book focused on sorcerers. Hunters Hunted 2 and KinfolkW20 both have some Hedge Magic but not any life extention stuff. WoD Ghosthunters is also going to have some Hedge Magic but again I dount it will have the life extention stuff. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar490_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"490\" data-vbnamecard=\"490\">omenseer</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T10:22:10-08:00","id":1421471,"title":"","content":"The librarian of Horizon - Nicodemus Mulhouse - in MtA is another example of a non-Mage with longevity due to Sorcery. He is over 600 years old.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1421348-mortal-life-extension-how#post1421348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides becoming a vampire or revenant, how could a mortal extend their life?<br /> <br /> I know mages can extend their life, but full immortality/agelessness is only high end.<br /> <br /> Lets say there is a mortal woman in her 70s who wants to extend her life. How could she go about doing it without becoming a vampire or a ghoul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pacts with Spirits, possibly going all the way up to the major Totems and higher Spirits Lords and Ladies.<br /> Magic items and artifacts.<br /> Infernal pacts.<br /> Pacts with the Wyrm - Banes, Black Spiral Dancers, Maeljin Incarnas, Urge-Wyrms et al. Remember that it is possible to be a Wyrm cultist without becoming a Fomor.<br /> Energy vampirism (it is a Sorcery Path in one of the books).<br /> Some rare events and achievements, like supping from a Fountain of Youth, bathing in a River of Life, or eating a Forever Fruit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-02-2020, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T10:55:50-08:00","id":1421475,"title":"","content":"You could also pretty easily hack the nWoD: Immortals into the oWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T11:44:30-08:00","id":1421486,"title":"","content":"WoD Ghost Hunters: Is that 20th or 5e?<br /> <br /> Good points on the spirit pacts. All very good ideas.<br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T12:13:33-08:00","id":1421489,"title":"","content":"WoD:GH is 20th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T13:31:34-08:00","id":1421502,"title":"","content":"Having lots of money lets you buy the best doctors available","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T17:55:10-08:00","id":1421707,"title":"","content":"Science, of the weird or hyper advanced variety. Depending on which game line's cosmology you prefer, this can take several different forms. IIRC, Werewolf's Book of the Weaver talks about the use of Weaver-spirit influenced and infused technology. With Mage, there's the Technocracy's Enlightened and Advanced Science (Sphere Magic and Path Sorcery, respectively), with their own versions of Life, Alchemy, and the like. I don't think Wraith ever really delved into that sort of thing, but it's entirely possible for some company or lab having discovered a way to harvest materials or energy from the Underworld into various drugs or other treatments. (IIRC, Orpheus involved something along those lines, but for the production of illegal narcotics.)<br /> <br /> Then there's just the idea of some sort of freak discovery of life extension. You can probably mine various science fiction films or shows for ideas. Things like Dead Heat (1988) and Second Chance (2016), for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T18:01:28-08:00","id":1421708,"title":"","content":"This is for a Vampire game, but I have added some lupine activity and some mage activity as well. Interestingly the coterie is on working terms with the Garou and the last member of a group of low magic users working for a Mage is now in the employ of the vampire who's aging wife is interested in extending her life.<br /> <br /> I have this thought of her going to the magic user for some 4 dot alchemy to giver her more time to work something out with the spirits. All while trying to keep her husband in the dark for the time being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T18:08:38-08:00","id":1421711,"title":"","content":"There is always infernalism. its a pretty standard contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T18:32:33-08:00","id":1421897,"title":"","content":"The archetypical one, I'd say.<br /> <br /> I'd swear I saw in one of the game books a plot about some organization using energies stolen or otherwise taken from ghosts to extend human life, with unpleasant results for all. Could it have been one of the <i>Orpheus</i> books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T22:21:15-08:00","id":1421932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1421348-mortal-life-extension-how?p=1421350#post1421350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if she's got the money and loose morals probably some sort of stem cell therapy</div> </div> </div> </div>Why'd you need loose morals to get your skins cells reprogrammed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T02:44:13-08:00","id":1421966,"title":"","content":"<i>The Picture of Dorian Gray</i> comes to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T18:49:35-08:00","id":1422162,"title":"","content":"Cursed (or otherwise darkly enchanted) objects. The old tv series Friday the 13th: The Series (which has nothing to do with the films; it was just a thing at the time, roll with it) had a couple of interesting possible ideas.<ul><li>An antique tea cup decorated with a Swapper's Ivy pattern that can take the life/youth of a drinker to give it to the cup's owner.</li> <li>An antique transport bee hive (which were made to transfer a hive from one location to another) which turns the bees into vampires, which drain the blood from victims and then transfer the life force to another person. (This is one of my favorites, just because the very idea of vampire bees is so batshit crazy I'm impressed someone thought of it.)</li> <li>A set of three carved monkeys in the See/Hear/Speak No Evil poses. The owner uses them to test the integrity of his children to see if they are worthy to inherit his estate. If they fail, they die, and their father continues to live until he eventually finds a worthy heir.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T12:32:22-08:00","id":1422638,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: There's a lot of disagreement over the exact 'limit' of the human lifespan. The general consensus I've seen is around 115-120, but some have argued 150 years or more (two scientists IIRC even have a bet ongoing whether people can live past the 'commonly believed' span.) A lot of it seems to come down to genetics, environment and probability (As in there are people who would exceed the 115-120 year 'limit' but they might be considered outliers rather than the norm.) <br /> <br /> Depending on how you wanted to define 'realism' and the variables in WoD you could just chalk it up to really good genetics or the effects of consensual reality (if you buy into that argument for your setting.) <br /> <br /> If you want a really far-fetched idea, what if certain strains of humans have been influenced by vampire blood (through ghouls, revenant or revenant-like beings, etc.) throughout millenia? You could get incremental improvements in lifespan like I described simply because of the effect vitae could have on human genetics. And that doesn't rule out other forms of magical 'influence' (hedge magic and alchemy, sphere magic, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T13:33:30-08:00","id":1422652,"title":"","content":"I am operating on the 80 limit at the moment. I am thinking she'll go to the hedge mage first and use that buy time to find something longer lasting and with less daily maintenance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}